 "literal": "If a person is of harsh words and without kindness, his great wealth, without enduring, will perish right there.",
 "translation": "If a ruler is harsh in speech and devoid of kindness, his vast wealth will perish instantly without enduring.",
 "modern": "கடுமையான சொற்களைப் பேசுபவனாகவும், இரக்கமற்றவனாகவும் ஒருவன் இருந்தால், அவனுடைய பெரிய செல்வம் நிலைத்து நிற்காமல் அப்பொழுதே அழிந்துவிடும்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet warns of the swift downfall of a leader who lacks basic virtues of speech and empathy. The word 'கண்' (eye) is used here in the sense of kindness or consideration. A ruler who speaks harshly ('கடுஞ்சொல்லன்') and lacks this kind consideration ('கண்ணிலன்') will find that even vast wealth ('நெடுஞ்செல்வம்') cannot save them. Without lasting long ('நீடின்றி'), their power and prosperity will vanish instantly ('ஆங்கே கெடும்') due to the resentment they foster.",
